{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q56450441","formula":"C₁₇H₂₃NO₃","hill":"C17H23NO3","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":17.0,"H":23.0,"N":1.0,"O":3.0},"names":{"en":"(-)-mesembrine","ru":"Мезембрин","uk":"(-)-Месембрін"},"descriptions":{"en":"Mesembrine is an alkaloid found within Sceletium tortuosum, commonly known as kanna. This compound is noted for its psychoactive properties, particularly as a serotonin reuptake inhibitor (SRI), which contributes to its potential use in treating mood disorders and anxiety. Mesembrine has garnered interest in both traditional medicine and modern pharmacology, where it is explored for its effects on enhancing mood and cognitive function.","ru":"Мезембрин (Месембрин) — алкалоид, содержащийся в Sceletium tortuosum. Мезембрин действует как ингибитор обратного захвата серотонина и как ингибитор фосфодиэстеразы 4 (PDE4). Таким образом, мезембрин может участвовать в механизмах антидепрессивного эффекта канны.","uk":"Месембрін (INN: Mesembrine) — інгібітор фосфодіестерази типу 4. Це алкалоїд, наявний у Sceletium tortuosum."},"fame":12,"pubchemCid":394162,"mass":289.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"CN1CC[C@]2([C@@H]1CC(=O)CC2)C3=CC(=C(C=C3)OC)OC","inchikey":"DAHIQPJTGIHDGO-IRXDYDNUSA-N","iupac":"(3aS,7aS)-3a-(3,4-dimethoxyphenyl)-1-methyl-2,3,4,5,7,7a-hexahydroindol-6-one","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"394162","atoms":44,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-3.551,"y":2.543,"z":0.966,"el":"O"},{"x":2.96,"y":1.3,"z":-1.442,"el":"O"},{"x":4.503,"y":-0.109,"z":0.391,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.177,"y":-0.854,"z":-0.884,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.146,"y":-0.766,"z":0.311,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.924,"y":-0.071,"z":-0.85,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.478,"y":-2.255,"z":0.036,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.765,"y":-0.359,"z":1.689,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.774,"y":-2.259,"z":-0.771,"el":"